<node id="11106939" title="Re^16: How do I display only matches" created="2019-10-02 04:03:23" updated="2019-10-02 04:03:23" _doctext_mode="strict"><type id="11">note</type>
<author id="830549">haukex</author>
<doctext field_name="doctext">&lt;blockquote&gt;&lt;i&gt;The &lt;c&gt;binmode FILEHANDLE&lt;/c&gt; operator in Perl is a no-op on POSIX&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Sorry, no - it still removes any non-default layers that may be present on the filehandle. Even a handle opened with the default &lt;c&gt;open my $fh, '&lt;', ...&lt;/c&gt; can have layers other than the normal defaults present due to the &lt;c&gt;PERLIO&lt;/c&gt; environment variable or the [https://perldoc.perl.org/open.html|open] pragma.&lt;/p&gt;
</doctext>
